The new look's UI type (docs/look/ui.md)

font.png   grey coverage atlas of the UI's glyphs, every baked size
font.txt   its metrics: faces, kerning pairs, bakes, glyph rectangles

Both are generated, not drawn: `python3.13 tools/look/ui_font.py` renders
them with FreeType (via Pillow) from two fonts:

  Carlito Bold   the sans, for the HUD's text
                 /usr/share/fonts/truetype/crosextra/Carlito-Bold.ttf
                 (Debian/Ubuntu package fonts-crosextra-carlito;
                 upstream https://github.com/googlefonts/carlito)
  Caladea Bold   the serif, for headings, counts and titles
                 /usr/share/fonts/truetype/crosextra/Caladea-Bold.ttf
                 (package fonts-crosextra-caladea;
                 upstream https://github.com/huertatipografica/Caladea)

Both are under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1: the fonts' own
name tables say so (licence description and URL, name IDs 13 and 14), as
do the packages' copyright files (/usr/share/doc/fonts-crosextra-*/
copyright). The atlas is a Modified Version of each under that licence and
is distributed under it; the copyright notices and the full licence text
are in OFL.txt beside this file. The atlas does not use either font's name
as its own, and is never sold by itself.
